.\" Keep this page current: it describes the demo game demos/madrun.bas (an executable made with BUILD, installed by "make install").
.TH ENGINE1999-MADRUN 6 "November 2026" "Engine 1999 @VERSION@" "Engine1999 Manual"
.SH NAME
engine1999-madrun \- MADRUN, a street crossing game for one to four players
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B engine1999-madrun
.SH DESCRIPTION
MADRUN is a crossing game for one to four players. A telephone is ringing in the booth on the island in the middle of a busy crossing: get there before the caller hangs up. Cars, trucks, buses, motorbikes and (later) ambulances drive on sixteen lanes (two in each direction on each of four roads); they stop for each other and for the crossings, but never for you. The four corners and the blocks between the roads are safe. If a vehicle hits you, you start again in a corner. The first player at the booth scores the level (more points for a fast answer); every level has more and faster traffic, and a call you miss costs everybody a life. Pick-ups: a whistle stops the traffic for five seconds, boots make you fast for ten seconds, a heart is an extra life. A close call scores 5 points.
.PP
The program is the demo \fImadrun.bas\fR of Engine1999, made into an executable with
.B BUILD
(window kind: it needs the SDL2 library, nothing else); its BASIC libraries are inside it. It opens the Engine1999 window; the window can
be switched between the full screen and a window with F11 or ALT+RETURN.
.SH CONTROLS
The game asks at the start for the keyboard (1 or 2 players) or for game controllers (up to 4: a controller that is connected brings its player, one that is removed takes it away).
.TP
.B Keyboard
player 1 moves with W A S D (with one player the cursor keys work, too), player 2 with the cursor keys.
.TP
.B Controllers
left stick or D-pad.
.TP
.B P
pause (START on a controller).
.TP
.B Q
quit (BACK on a controller).
.SH FILES
The high score is kept in the file
.I madrun.hi
in the current directory (the game goes on without it if the file cannot be written).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR engine1999 (1),
.BR engine1999-basic (7)
